Bound aggregate SVG render memory and dash expansion per render.

Telegram-originated hardening, not an upstream backport. Each image QtSvg
allocates for a filter, mask, pattern or offscreen buffer is limited only by
the per-image allocation limit, but an untrusted document could keep one
filter region image alive per distinct result name and one buffer per nested
filtered element, many gigabytes in total. Untrusted SVG repeating dashed
segments over many paths, references and nested offscreen images could also
emit hundreds of millions of dashes from a few kilobytes.

For untrusted documents reserve every such image, the transient workspace
of each filter primitive and the dash loop iterations of QDashStroker and
of the raster engine dashed lines, from budgets owned by the document
before they are allocated, and return them when the last copy of the image
is destroyed.
